A table takes a slot more than its count wherever the kernel counts it, so the walks agree with the allocator,
and only the structure's own size, 12 bytes and 24 a slot rounded to eight as the manual gives it, tells the error,
in the untraced prologue's table already.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: an object took other bytes than its type takes

diff --git a/kernel/object.h b/kernel/object.h
--- a/kernel/object.h
+++ b/kernel/object.h
@@ -609,7 +609,7 @@ static inline size_t obj_type_size(uint8_t type, uint32_t slots)
